%29.jpeg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original", "descriptionurl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlas_Van_der_Hagen-KW1049B12_029-DIOECESE_de_RHEIMS_et_le_pa%C3%AFs_de_RETHEL_(%C3%A9pernay).jpeg", "descriptionshorturl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/page/83462670", "extmetadata": {"DateTime": {"value": "2019-10-28 14:59:14", "source": "mediawiki-metadata", "hidden": ""}, "ObjectName": {"value": "<div class=\"fn\">\nDIOECESE de RHEIMS et le païs de RETHEL</div>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "CommonsMetadataExtension": {"value": 1.2, "source": "extension", "hidden": ""}, "Categories": {"value": "Media contributed by Koninklijke Bibliotheek|Parc naturel régional de la Montagne de Reims|Louvois (Marne)|Roman Catholic Archdiocese of Reims|Maps of Épernay|Ville-en-Selve|Maps of Avenay-Val-d'Or|PD-Art (PD-old-100)|Artworks with Wikidata item|Artworks with known accession number|Extracted images|CC-PD-Mark|1635 maps of France|GWToolset Batch Upload|Atlas van der Hagen|Artworks with Wikidata item missing author|Artworks with Wikidata item missing genre|Artworks digital representation of unknown type of work|Atlas van der Hagen - Extracted images|Maps of Taissy (Marne)|Atlas van der Hagen (Volume 3)", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "Assessments": {"value": "", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "Artist": {"value": "<bdi><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:Joan_Blaeu\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:Joan Blaeu\"><span title=\"Dutch cartographer (1596-1673)\">Joan Blaeu</span></a></bdi> / <bdi><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:Willem_Blaeu\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:Willem Blaeu\"><span title=\"Dutch cartographer, atlas maker and publisher (1571-1638)\">Willem Blaeu</span></a></bdi>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "ImageDescription": {"value": "A map of the French episcopate Reims and the region Rethel was published by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willem_Blaeu\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Willem Blaeu\">Willem Jansz. Blaeu</a> (1571-1638) and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joan_Blaeu\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Joan Blaeu\">Joan Blaeu</a> (1598-1673). The map was composed using two detailed maps by the French cartographer Jean Jubrien, which were published earlier by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henricus_Hondius_II\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Henricus Hondius II\">Henricus Hondius II</a> (1597-1651) and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melchior_Tavernier\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Melchior Tavernier\">Melchior Tavernier</a> . The extent of the two original maps is clearly visible in the density of details on Blaeus map.", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "DateTimeOriginal": {"value": "1635<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P571,+1635-00-00T00:00:00Z/9</div>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Credit": {"value": "This digital media file - and/or the physical objects depicted on it - originates from the digital and/or physical collections of the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.kb.nl/\">Koninklijke Bibliotheek</a>, national library of the Netherlands.", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Permission": {"value": "<table cellspacing=\"8\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; background-color: var(--background-color-interactive, #f0f0f0); color: inherit; border: 2px solid var(--border-color-subtle, #e0e0e0); width:100%;\" class=\"layouttemplate\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>\n<div class=\"center\">This is a faithful photographic reproduction of a two-dimensional, <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Public_domain\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Public domain\">public domain</a> work of art. The work of art itself is in the public domain for the following reason:</div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">\n<table class=\"licensetpl\" style=\"display:none\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><span class=\"licensetpl_short\">Public domain</span><span